d Health Research Unit, Institute of Agrochemistry and Food Technology, National Research Council, Paterna-Valencia 46980, Spain."}]}}, {"fullName": "Hausken T", "lastName": "Hausken", "firstName": "Trygve", "initials": "T", "authorAffiliationDetailsList": {"authorAffiliation": [{"affiliation": "Department of Clinical Medicine, University of Bergen, Bergen 5021, Norway."}]}}, {"fullName": "Lied GA", "lastName": "Lied", "firstName": "Gülen Arslan", "initials": "GA", "authorAffiliationDetailsList": {"authorAffiliation": [{"affiliation": "National Center for Functional Gastrointestinal Disorders, Department of Medicine, Haukeland University Hospital, Bergen 5021, Norway."}]}}, {"fullName": "Lundervold A", "lastName": "Lundervold", "firstName": "Arvid", "initials": "A", "authorId": {"type": "ORCID", "value": "0000-0002-0032-4182"}, "authorAffiliationDetailsList": {"authorAffiliation": [{"affiliation": "Mohn Medical Imaging and Visualization Center, Department of Radiology, Haukeland University Hospital, Bergen 5021, Norway."}]}}, {"fullName": "Berentsen B", "lastName": "Berentsen", "firstName": "Birgitte", "initials": "B", "authorId": {"type": "ORCID", "value": "0000-0003-3574-7078"}, "authorAffiliationDetailsList": {"authorAffiliation": [{"affiliation": "Department of Clinical Medicine, University of Bergen, Bergen 5021, Norway."}]}}]}, "authorIdList": {"authorId": [{"type": "ORCID", "value": "0000-0001-5707-4340"}, {"type": "ORCID", "value": "0000-0002-0032-4182"}, {"type": "ORCID", "value": "0000-0002-1615-1976"}, {"type": "ORCID", "value": "0000-0002-4155-294X"}, {"type": "ORCID", "value": "0000-0002-6043-819X"}, {"type": "ORCID", "value": "0000-0003-3574-7078"}]}, "dataLinksTagsList": {"dataLinkstag": ["altmetrics", "supporting_data"]}, "journalInfo": {"issue": "4", "volume": "28", "journalIssueId": 3305862, "dateOfPublication": "2022 Jan", "monthOfPublication": 1, "yearOfPublication": 2022, "journal": {"medlineAbbreviation": "World J Gastroenterol", "title": "World journal of gastroenterology", "essn": "2219-2840", "issn": "1007-9327", "nlmid": "100883448", "isoabbreviation": "World J Gastroenterol"}, "printPublicationDate": "2022-01-01"}, "pubYear": "2022", "pageInfo": "412-431", "abstractText": "Irritable bowel syndrome (IBS) is a common clinical label for medically unexplained gastrointestinal symptoms, recently described as a disturbance of the microbiota-gut-brain axis. Despite decades of research, the pathophysiology of this highly heterogeneous disorder remains elusive. However, a dramatic change in the understanding of the underlying pathophysiological mechanisms surfaced when the importance of gut microbiota protruded the scientific picture. Are we getting any closer to understanding IBS' etiology, or are we drowning in unspecific, conflicting data because we possess limited tools to unravel the cluster of secrets our gut microbiota is concealing? In this comprehensive review we are discussing some of the major important features of IBS and their interaction with gut microbiota, clinical microbiota-altering treatment such as the low FODMAP diet and fecal microbiota transplantation, neuroimaging and methods in microbiota analyses, and current and future challenges with big data analysis in IBS.", "affiliation": "Department of Clinical Medicine, University of Bergen, Bergen 5021, Norway.", "publicationStatus": "ppublish", "language": "eng", "pubModel": "Print", "pubTypeList": {"pubType": ["review-article", "Review", "Journal Article"]}, "meshHeadingList": {"meshHeading": [{"majorTopic_YN": "N", "descriptorName": "Humans"}, {"majorTopic_YN": "Y", "descriptorName": "Irritable Bowel Syndrome", "meshQualifierList": {"meshQualifier": [{"majorTopic_YN": "N", "abbreviation": "TH", "qualifierName": "therapy"}]}}, {"majorTopic_YN": "Y", "descriptorName": "Microbiota"}, {"majorTopic_YN": "Y", "descriptorName": "Gastrointestinal Microbiome"}, {"majorTopic_YN": "N", "descriptorName": "Fecal Microbiota Transplantation"}, {"majorTo